# Nginx Performance Fixes

## Overview

This document contains critical Nginx configuration changes to fix performance issues in the frontend-to-backend connection path. These changes eliminate connection overhead, enable compression, and improve throughput.

**Impact:** Expected 50-200ms TTFB improvement per request, 70-90% payload reduction for JSON responses, and major throughput gains under load.

**Priority:** P0 - Critical (implement immediately)

---

## A1. Fix Next.js Keepalive (Connection 'upgrade' kills keepalive)

**File:** `/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/infinitycolor.org` (Next.js location block)

**Problem:** `Connection 'upgrade'` is hardcoded on every request, not just WebSocket upgrades. This tells the upstream to close the connection after each response. The `keepalive 32` directive in the upstream block is completely nullified.

**Current (BROKEN):**
```nginx
location / {
    proxy_pass http://next_upstream;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';  # <-- KILLS keepalive
    # ... other headers
}
```

**Fix:**
```nginx
# At the top of the file, ensure this map exists (already defined for gitlab):
map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {
    default upgrade;
    ''      close;
}

location / {
    proxy_pass http://next_upstream;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;  # "" for normal, "upgrade" for WS
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;

    # Enable buffering for better throughput
    proxy_buffering on;
    proxy_buffers 16 16k;
    proxy_buffer_size 16k;
}
```

**Impact:** Eliminates TCP handshake overhead (~1-3ms per request). With 5 Next.js instances serving hundreds of concurrent requests, this adds up to seconds of cumulative latency.

