## B1. Internal Strapi URL (Nginx Internal Server Block)

**Problem:** Next.js server-side fetches go through the public domain, adding DNS + TLS + extra Nginx hop overhead (50-200ms per fetch).

**Solution:** Create an internal-only Nginx server block that bypasses TLS:

**File:** `/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/infinitycolor.org` (or create new file)

```nginx
# Internal-only server block for Next.js -> Strapi communication (no TLS)
server {
    listen 127.0.0.1:8080;
    server_name localhost;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://strapi_upstream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Connection "";  # Enable keepalive
        proxy_set_header Host api.infinitycolor.co;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        
        # Buffering
        proxy_buffering on;
        proxy_buffers 16 16k;
        proxy_buffer_size 16k;
        
        # Timeouts
        proxy_read_timeout 600s;
        proxy_connect_timeout 600s;
        proxy_send_timeout 600s;
    }
}
```

**Environment Variable:** Add to Next.js production environment (`.env` or deployment config):

```bash
STRAPI_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/api
```

**Impact:** Eliminates DNS lookup + TLS handshake + double Nginx proxy. Expected TTFB improvement: 50-200ms per server-side fetch.

